+/**
+ * Schlick Fresnel whose grazing reflectance is capped at (1 - perceptual roughness)² (never below F0), a stronger
+ * form of Lagarde's roughness-aware Schlick (the linear cap still left stone 16% darker at 4 degrees on the rig):
+ * a rough block seen at a grazing angle stays mostly
+ * diffuse instead of turning into a grey mirror of the sky. With the plain rise the diffuse layer under it kept only
+ * (1 - F): about 30% of its colour at 4 degrees, the grey veil over blocks seen at an angle (owner 29.10).
+ */
+float3 surfaceFresnelRough(float cosine, float3 f0, float alphaRoughness) {
+    float m = clamp(1.0 - cosine, 0.0, 1.0);
+    float m2 = m * m;
+    float smoothness = 1.0 - sqrt(alphaRoughness);
